1672 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 996 0 R
/E (The Social Media Addiction Analyzer is a data-driven system developed to analyze the impact of excessive social media usage on students' productivity, mental health, sleep quality, and academic performance. Using a Kaggle dataset of 705 students with 13 demographic and behavioral attributes, the data was preprocessed through cleaning, duplicate removal, and feature selection to ensure analytical reliability. Interactive Power BI dashboards provide insights into addiction distribution, platform-wise usage, mental health correlations, demographic patterns, and behavioral trends, revealing that a majority of students fall into the high addiction category and that higher social media usage is associated with poorer mental health and academic outcomes. The dashboard spans four report pages covering KPI summaries, platform risk analysis, conflict escalation patterns, geographic usage distribution, and a platform-by-gender insights matrix. The findings demonstrate how business intelligence and visual analytics can support digital well-being awareness and informed decision-making in educational environments.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
