/Title (The rapid proliferation of social media platforms has fundamentally transformed how young people communicate, learn, and spend their time. Platforms such as Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, Facebook, and WhatsApp have become deeply embedded in the daily routines of students and adolescents across the world. While these platforms offer genuine benefits in terms of connectivity, self-expression, and information access, their excessive and unregulated use has emerged as a serious public health concern.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5483 0 R
/Next 5504 0 R
>>
endobj
