5509 0 obj
<<
/Title (The consequences of this addiction are wide-ranging. Studies have consistently shown a negative correlation between social media addiction and mental health outcomes, including elevated levels of anxiety, depression, loneliness, and diminished self-esteem. Sleep deprivation is another critical consequence, as late-night scrolling and screen exposure disrupt natural sleep cycles, which in turn further deteriorates mental health and academic focus. Academically, students addicted to social media are more likely to experience poor concentration, procrastination, lower grades, and reduced motivation.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5483 0 R
/Prev 5504 0 R
/Next 5505 0 R
>>
endobj
